The '''Three threats of Fosia''' referred to the countries of [[Mitoyagi]], [[Zong]] and [[Nakamizu]] that were the core industrial and military power centers of Fosia. The term was coined by Volisanian politician [[Ernesto Bonastre]] in 1878. The three nations between the period of 1850-1895 has the strongest period of industrial, economic and military growth in Adonia, followed by at the time [[Volisania]], [[Burawa]], [[Merica]] and [[Daras]]. 

The reference to their "threat" was keyed more to their large military and economic influence over [[Lurandia]] and possibility of a looming invasion by one of those powers over Illpynian allied nations in new world. The threat came to reality during the [[Second War of the Isthmus]] as Zong and allied [[Louyang]] and [[Sinchew]] forces were able to expand their territory into modern day Balboa and occupy major ports by the end of the conflict in 1899.